D3D12: acceleration-structure memory is reported aligned to 256.

GetAccelerationStructureMemoryDesc2 and AccelerationStructureD3D12::GetMemoryDesc size the
structure as a plain buffer, and on a device with tight alignment a buffer's alignment drops to 128,
below D3D12_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_BYTE_ALIGNMENT, which an acceleration structure's
address needs and memoryAlignment.accelerationStructureOffset reports. NRI validation checks a
placement against the reported alignment, so a 128-aligned placement passes it and fails later.
Since 3371cdb, which replaced accelerationStructureOffsetAlignment with the buffer's alignment.

This raises the reported alignment to D3D12_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_BYTE_ALIGNMENT.
Micromaps are left as they are: 128 is their own alignment
(D3D12_RAYTRACING_OPACITY_MICROMAP_ARRAY_BYTE_ALIGNMENT).
Measured on v190, NVIDIA, Agility 1.619: BLAS and TLAS memory reported aligned to 128; a TLAS placed
at 2,688 after a BLAS passed NRI validation, and its descriptor was refused: "[31]
ID3D12Device::TryCreateShaderResourceView: For D3D12_SRV_DIMENSION_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE,
the address (...) must be aligned to 256 bytes." Vulkan reports 256. With the change D3D12 reports
256, and a BLAS and a TLAS placed in one allocation at the reported alignment trace like committed
ones.

diff --git a/Source/D3D12/AccelerationStructureD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/AccelerationStructureD3D12.hpp
index 8c55a1c..028fcb5 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/AccelerationStructureD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/AccelerationStructureD3D12.hpp
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@ void AccelerationStructureD3D12::GetMemoryDesc(MemoryLocation memoryLocation, Me
     D3D12_RESOURCE_DESC1 resourceDesc = {};
     m_Device.GetResourceDesc(bufferDesc, resourceDesc);
     m_Device.GetMemoryDesc(memoryLocation, resourceDesc, memoryDesc);
+    memoryDesc.alignment = std::max(memoryDesc.alignment, (uint32_t)D3D12_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_BYTE_ALIGNMENT); // a tightly aligned buffer may be less
 }
 
 NRI_INLINE void AccelerationStructureD3D12::SetDebugName(const char* name) {
